elease history showed v2.3.0 as the most recent release that was healthy in production (v2.3.1-rc was a staging-only, unhealthy build, so I excluded it).\n- **Rollback to v2.3.0:** The first attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving a mixed state. I retried, and the second attempt completed in all three regions. Post-rollback the service is **healthy** with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** Opened **INC-0001 (SEV2)** for checkout-api. The first create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying to avoid a duplicate page \u2014 it had been created successfully. The summary covers the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the recovery, and follow-ups.\n\n**Follow-ups for the on-call engineer:** root-cause the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy (worth noting the RC was also unhealthy in staging), and look into the orchestrator error that caused the partial rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}